  "live_records": {
    "q-77200": {
      "dom_id": "step-q77200",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the equivalence relation $∼$ on $R,$ defined by $x∼y$ if ${x}^{3}={y}^{3}.$ Which of the following are in the equivalence class $[8]?$\n\nI. $-2$\n\nII. $2$\n\nIII. $8$",
      "worked_solution": "The equivalence class $[8]$ consists of the elements that are equivalent to $8$ under the given equivalence relation. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[8] & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,x∼8} \\\\  & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,{x}^{3}={8}^{3}} \\\\  & ={x\\in R\\,|\\,x=8} \\\\  & ={8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $8$ is in $[8],$ while $-2$ and $2$ are not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
